CSV Downloadables:
particle_timeseries_*.csv — every frame, every particle: vdiam_px/um, major/minor, Taylor, velocity, dD/dt
particle_peak_analysis_*.csv — one row per particle: T before/at/after, ΔT, V before/after, velocity delta, vdiam stats, τ
particle_size_distribution_*.csv — mean/std of vdiam, major, minor, Taylor per particle

User Note: The table has multiple columns, extend the horizontal scroll bar to see them all.  The "T before/at/after" columns show the Taylor parameter 1 frame before, at, and 1 frame after the confirmed peak frame.  ΔT is the difference between after and before (signed).  V before/after are the velocities in µm/s one frame before and after the peak frame.  Velocity delta is the difference between after and before (signed).  The vdiam stats column shows the mean and std of vertical diameter across all frames for that particle.  τ is the viscoelastic relaxation time computed from post-peak Taylor decay, if available.
